    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "lu6we",
      "x": 6400,
      "y": 7240,
      "name": "f56Lbl",
      "fill": "#00FF9C",
      "content": "56 · BACKEND PAGINATION — FLUSH PAGER",
      "fontFamily": "JetBrains Mono",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontWeight": "700",
      "letterSpacing": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "hNttf",
      "x": 2780,
      "y": 8360,
      "name": "56 notes",
      "width": 720,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Feature 56 / #377 — backend pagination + honest bottom pager\n\n• Paging moves into SQL: list commands take page / page_size / query (LIMIT/OFFSET, LIKE over the fields client search covered) and return items + filtered_count + total_count. Counter = page items of filtered.\n• Pager STAYS bottom-pinned and centered, unchanged position. What changes: a 1px hairline ($border) separates it from the list, and the list region above scrolls with a VISIBLE auto-hiding scrollbar — a card cut at the fold reads as a scrollable region above a fixed footer, not as content swallowed by a black block; its hairline aligns with the sidebar footer's divider (one continuous line) (left frame: 6th card at the fold + scrollbar thumb).\n• Single page: the pager STAYS visible — page 1 selected, both arrows disabled — so the footer and its aligned divider persist; the disabled arrows say \"nothing more\" without implying hidden pages. No separate frame needed.\n• cmp/Pager unchanged — 28px controls were already slim.\n"
    },
